{"pageProps": {"params": {"versionId": "59", "usfm": "AMO.5.ESV"}, "audioVersionInfo": {"title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "copyright_long": {"text": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament", "html": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament"}, "copyright_short": {"text": "\u2117 2016 Crossway", "html": "<p>\u2117 2016 Crossway</p>"}, "version_id": 59, "id": 1, "publisher_link": "", "dramatized": false, "publisher": {"id": 575, "name": "Hear Book Audio", "local_name": "Hear Book Audio", "url": null, "description": null}}, "type": "chapter", "chapterInfo": {"audioChapterInfo": [{"download_urls": {"format_mp3_32k": "//audio-bible-cdn.youversionapi.com/1/32k/AMO/5-eea08359ca3a79076b6b54d9d1fe7831.mp3?version_id=59", "format_hls": "//audio-hls.youversionapi.com/1/m4a/32k/AMO/5-eea08359ca3a79076b6b54d9d1fe7831.m3u8?version_id=59"}, "id": 1, "version_id": 59, "title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "timing_available": true, "dramatized": false, "default": true}], "content": "<div class=\"version vid59 iso6393eng\" data-vid=\"59\" data-iso6393=\"eng\">\n    <div class=\"book bkAMO\">\n        <div class=\"chapter ch5\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5\">\n            <div class=\"label\">5</div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">Seek the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"heading\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"heading\"> and Live</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"verse v1\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.1\"><span class=\"label\">1</span><span class=\"content\">Hear this word that I </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ezek. 19:1</span></span><span class=\"content\">take up over you in lamentation, O house of Israel:</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v1\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.1\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.2\"><span class=\"label\">2</span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Fallen, no more to rise,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.2\"><span class=\"content\">is </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Lam. 2:1; [Isa. 47:1]</span></span><span class=\"content\">the virgin Israel;</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.2\"><span class=\"content\">forsaken on her land,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.2\"><span class=\"content\">with none to raise her up.&#8221;</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"m\"><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.2\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.3\"><span class=\"label\">3</span><span class=\"content\">For thus says the Lord </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">God</span></span><span class=\"content\">:</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.3\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;The city that went out a thousand</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.3\"><span class=\"content\">shall have a hundred left,</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.3\"><span class=\"content\">and that which went out a hundred</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.3\"><span class=\"content\">shall have ten left</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.3\"><span class=\"content\">to the house of Israel.&#8221;</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"m\"><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.3\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.4\"><span class=\"label\">4</span><span class=\"content\">For thus says the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> to the house of Israel:</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.4\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        2 Chr. 15:2; Isa. 55:6; Zeph. 2:3  </span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Seek me and live;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.4\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.5\"><span class=\"label\">5</span><span class=\"content\">but do not seek </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See ch. 4:4 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Bethel,</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.5\"><span class=\"content\">and do not enter into </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See ch. 4:4 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Gilgal</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.5\"><span class=\"content\">or cross over to </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 8:14</span></span><span class=\"content\">Beersheba;</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.5\"><span class=\"content\">for </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See ch. 4:4 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Gilgal shall surely go into exile,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.5\"><span class=\"content\">and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See ch. 4:4 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Bethel shall come to nothing.&#8221;</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.5\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.6\"><span class=\"label\">6</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [See ver. 4 above]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Seek the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> and live,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.6\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [Isa. 9:18, 19]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">lest he break out like fire in the house of Joseph,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.6\"><span class=\"content\">and it devour, with none to quench it for </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 5 above]</span></span><span class=\"content\">Bethel,</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.6\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.7\"><span class=\"label\">7</span><span class=\"content\">O </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 6:12]</span></span><span class=\"content\">you who turn justice to wormwood</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">5:7 </span><span class=\"ft\">Or </span><span class=\"fq\">to bitter fruit</span></span></span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.7\"><span class=\"content\">and cast down righteousness to the earth!</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.7\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.8\"><span class=\"label\">8</span><span class=\"content\">He who made the </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Job 9:9; 38:31 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Pleiades and Orion,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.8\"><span class=\"content\">and turns deep darkness into the morning</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.8\"><span class=\"content\">and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 104:20; [ch. 4:13; 8:9] </span></span><span class=\"content\">darkens the day into night,</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.8\"><span class=\"content\">who </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 9:6; [Gen. 6:17; Ps. 104:6, 7] </span></span><span class=\"content\">calls for the waters of the sea</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.8\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    ch. 9:6; [Gen. 6:17; Ps. 104:6, 7]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">and pours them out on the surface of the earth,</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.8\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    See ch. 4:13  </span></span><span class=\"content\">the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> is his name;</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.8\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v9\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.9\"><span class=\"label\">9</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [Jer. 50:32]  </span></span><span class=\"content\">who makes destruction flash forth against the strong,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v9\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.9\"><span class=\"content\">so that destruction comes upon the fortress.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v9\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.9\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.10\"><span class=\"label\">10</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Isa. 29:21; [Prov. 15:5, 10]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">They hate him who reproves </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Ruth 4:1 </span></span><span class=\"content\">in the gate,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.10\"><span class=\"content\">and they </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[1 Kgs. 22:8]</span></span><span class=\"content\">abhor him who speaks the truth.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.10\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.11\"><span class=\"label\">11</span><span class=\"content\">Therefore because you </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[James 2:6] </span></span><span class=\"content\">trample on</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">5:11 </span><span class=\"ft\">Or </span><span class=\"fq\">you tax</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> the poor</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.11\"><span class=\"content\">and you exact taxes of grain from him,</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.11\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Deut. 28:30, 39; Mic. 6:15; Zeph. 1:13  </span></span><span class=\"content\">you have built houses of hewn stone,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.11\"><span class=\"content\">but you shall not dwell in them;</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.11\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Deut. 28:30, 39; Mic. 6:15; Zeph. 1:13  </span></span><span class=\"content\">you have planted pleasant vineyards,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.11\"><span class=\"content\">but you shall not drink their wine.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.11\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.12\"><span class=\"label\">12</span><span class=\"content\">For I know how many are your transgressions</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.12\"><span class=\"content\">and how great are your sins&#8212;</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.12\"><span class=\"content\">you who afflict the righteous, who </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">1 Sam. 8:3; 12:3; [Ps. 26:10] </span></span><span class=\"content\">take a bribe,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.12\"><span class=\"content\">and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 2:7; Isa. 29:21 </span></span><span class=\"content\">turn aside the needy </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 10 above]</span></span><span class=\"content\">in the gate.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.12\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v13\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.13\"><span class=\"label\">13</span><span class=\"content\">Therefore he who is prudent will </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Eccles. 3:7] </span></span><span class=\"content\">keep silent in such a time,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v13\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.13\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Mic. 2:3\n        </span></span><span class=\"content\">for it is an evil time.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v13\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.13\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.14\"><span class=\"label\">14</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [Deut. 30:15, 19; Zeph. 2:3]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Seek good, and not evil,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.14\"><span class=\"content\">that you may live;</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.14\"><span class=\"content\">and so the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 3:13</span></span><span class=\"content\">the God of hosts, will be with you,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.14\"><span class=\"content\">as you have said.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.14\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.15\"><span class=\"label\">15</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Ps. 97:10; Rom. 12:9   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Hate evil, and love good,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.15\"><span class=\"content\">and establish justice </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 10 above] </span></span><span class=\"content\">in the gate;</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.15\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Joel 2:14; [Ex. 32:30]  </span></span><span class=\"content\">it may be that the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">, the God of hosts,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.15\"><span class=\"content\">will be gracious to the remnant of Joseph.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"m\"><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.15\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.16\"><span class=\"label\">16</span><span class=\"content\">Therefore thus says the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 14 above] </span></span><span class=\"content\">the God of hosts, the Lord:</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.16\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;In all the squares </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Jer. 9:17, 18]</span></span><span class=\"content\">there shall be wailing,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.16\"><span class=\"content\">and in all the streets they shall say, &#8216;Alas! Alas!&#8217;</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.16\"><span class=\"content\">They shall call the farmers to mourning</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.16\"><span class=\"content\">and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Jer. 9:17, 18]</span></span><span class=\"content\">to wailing those who are skilled in lamentation,</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.16\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.17\"><span class=\"label\">17</span><span class=\"content\">and in all vineyards there shall be wailing,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.17\"><span class=\"content\">for </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ex. 12:12</span></span><span class=\"content\">I will pass through your midst,&#8221;</span></span></div><div class=\"qr\"><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.17\"><span class=\"content\">says the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">.</span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">Let Justice Roll Down</span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.17\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v18\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.18\"><span class=\"label\">18</span><span class=\"content\">Woe to you who desire </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Joel 1:15 </span></span><span class=\"content\">the day of the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">!</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v18\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.18\"><span class=\"content\">Why would you have the day of the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">?</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v18\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.18\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    See Joel 2:1, 2  </span></span><span class=\"content\">It is darkness, and not light,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v18\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.18\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v19\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.19\"><span class=\"label\">19</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [Isa. 24:18; Jer. 48:44]  </span></span><span class=\"content\">as if a man fled from a lion,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v19\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.19\"><span class=\"content\">and a bear met him,</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v19\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.19\"><span class=\"content\">or went into the house and leaned his hand against the wall,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v19\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.19\"><span class=\"content\">and a serpent bit him.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v19\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.19\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v20\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.20\"><span class=\"label\">20</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [See ver. 18 above]  </span></span><span class=\"content\">Is not the day of the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> darkness, and not light,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v20\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.20\"><span class=\"content\">and gloom with no brightness in it?</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v20\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.20\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v21\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.21\"><span class=\"label\">21</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Isa. 1:14; [Jer. 6:20]  </span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;I hate, I despise your feasts,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v21\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.21\"><span class=\"content\">and I take no delight in your solemn assemblies.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v21\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.21\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v22\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.22\"><span class=\"label\">22</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Ps. 51:16, 17; Isa. 1:11  </span></span><span class=\"content\">Even though you offer me your burnt offerings and grain offerings,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v22\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.22\"><span class=\"content\">I will not accept them;</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v22\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.22\"><span class=\"content\">and the peace offerings of your fattened animals,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v22\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.22\"><span class=\"content\">I will not look upon them.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v22\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.22\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v23\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.23\"><span class=\"label\">23</span><span class=\"content\">Take away from me the noise of your songs;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v23\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.23\"><span class=\"content\">to </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 6:5; 8:3; Isa. 5:12]</span></span><span class=\"content\">the melody of your harps I will not listen.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v23\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.23\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v24\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.24\"><span class=\"label\">24</span><span class=\"content\">But let justice roll down like waters,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v24\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.24\"><span class=\"content\">and righteousness like an ever-flowing stream.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v24\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.24\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v25\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.25\"><span class=\"label\">25</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    Cited Acts 7:42, 43  </span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Did you bring to me sacrifices and offerings during the forty years in the wilderness, O house of Israel? </span></span><span class=\"verse v26\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.26\"><span class=\"label\">26</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Deut. 32:17; Ezek. 20:16, 24] </span></span><span class=\"content\">You </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Isa. 46:7]</span></span><span class=\"content\">shall take up Sikkuth your king, and Kiyyun your star-god&#8212;your images that you made for yourselves, </span></span><span class=\"verse v27\" data-usfm=\"AMO.5.27\"><span class=\"label\">27</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">2 Kgs. 17:6 </span></span><span class=\"content\">and I will send you into exile beyond Damascus,&#8221; says the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">, whose name is </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 14 above]</span></span><span class=\"content\">the God of hosts.</span></span></div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div>", "copyright": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers.</p>", "text": "The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV